                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.6363 Am 6/68: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-03-07T21:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 7, 1921—9
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 8(<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >?</hi>)—11:47 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>42. Congress this evening rejected Amory concession protocol by 24 to 10 votes.
                    Will report promptly any consequences.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
